    "controls": "y",
    "capability_check": "y",
    "uncertainty_reported": "n",
    "code_released": "not stated",
    "peer_reviewed": "Proceedings of the 9th MLSys Conference, 2026",
    "problems": "Only one 4B model was fine-tuned, and the authors report no multi-seed repetitions. The tasks are procedural and the paper did not evaluate transfer to natural-language benchmarks. The results use test accuracy rather than pretraining loss and do not fit power laws. Compute was fixed, and graph-task outcomes were affected by generation-length limits and incomplete rollouts.",
    "rows_left_out": "No reported held-out pretraining-loss, power-law-fit, extrapolation, or compute-optimal-allocation results were present. Training and validation reward trajectories and per-difficulty or query-type breakdowns are not included because they do not measure the claim's named outcomes.",
